[32.733622, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[2d\u001b[38;5;237;48;5;252;1m  \u001b[m\u001b[5;3H\u001b[38;5;252mto declare.\u001b[m\u001b[6;105H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252mDivision for the two.\u001b[m\u001b[25X\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;252mImplementer\u001b[m\u001b[90X\u001b[10;105H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m1.\u001b[38;5;252m State the interface first — command name, \u001b[48;5;234m--threshold\u001b[49m default, one line per\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   below-threshold item, exit behavior — so there's a contract to review.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m2.\u001b[38;5;252m Write the CLI: read \u001b[48;5;234mitem,quantity\u001b[49m, compare each quantity to the threshold, print the\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   low items.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m3.\u001b[38;5;252m Cover the edges: missing/unreadable file, bad header, non-numeric quantity, empty\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   result, with sane exit codes.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m4.\u001b[38;5;252m Add tests over a couple of fixtures including the repo's \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1597/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\u001b[m\u001b[32X\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m5.\u001b[38;5;252m Hand over script, tests, and the exact commands to run both.\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5;252mReviewer\u001b[m\u001b[75X\u001b[21;105H\u001b[1K\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m1.\u001b[38;5;252m Read the declared acceptance, then run the CLI and tests independently.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m2.\u001b[38;5;252m Probe what the tests don't: threshold boundary (is a quantity exactly equal\u001b[m\u001b[23X\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   included?), flag vs default, malformed CSV, empty pantry.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m3.\u001b[38;5;252m Review against the repo's own fixture and report any counterexample with the exact\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;252m   command.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;102m4.\u001b[38;5;252m Give one verdict — holds or does not — plus the single refuting case if it fails.\u001b[m\r\n\n  \u001b[38;5