[208.033527, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[26;37r\u001b[37;1H\u001b[4S\u001b[1;42r\u001b[6;31H\u001b[K\n\u001b[38;5;146m› \u001b[38;5;110mBuild a practical pantry stock-report CLI in this project. Start an implementer named builder to create\u001b[m\u001b[8;33H\u001b[38;5;110mpantry.py using Python standard library and unittest tests. Use item,quantity CSV, default threshold 3,\u001b[m\u001b[9;33H\u001b[38;5;110mstrict below, alphabetical output, nonzero exit on malformed rows. Have builder run the CLI and tests and\u001b[m\u001b[10;33H\u001b[38;5;110mreport back. Then start a separate reviewer to inspect and run the result independently. Keep all buying\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[11;33H\u001b[38;5;110mand inventory edits manual. Tell me when each handoff is complete.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[13;31H  \u001b[38;5;243m▸ worked 6.7s · thought 3.1s · 3 steps · 5 tool calls · ctrl+e\u001b[m\u001b[15;31H\u001b[38;5;252mHandoff 1 is in flight. I started the implementer \u001b[38;5;146;4m@builder\u001b[38;5;252;24m with a fixed interface:\u001b[m\u001b[16;31H\u001b[38;5;252;48;5;234mpython3 pantry.py CSV [--threshold N]\u001b[49m, default threshold 3, \u001b[48;5;234mitem,quantity\u001b[49m CSV,\u001b[m\u001b[17;31H\u001b[38;5;252mstrictly-below test, alphabetical \u001b[48;5;234mitem: quantity\u001b[49m output, exit 2 on malformed rows, and a\u001b[m\u001b[18;31H\u001b[38;5;252mhard read-only constraint (no inventory writes, edits stay manual). It's writing\u001b[m\u001b[19;31H\u001b[38;5;252mpantry.py plus unittest tests, then running the CLI and the tests and reporting raw\u001b[m\u001b[20;31H\u001b[38;5;252moutput.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[21;31H\u001b[83X\n\u001b[38;5;252mI'll start the reviewer the moment builder reports back, and tell you when each handoff\u001b[m\u001b[23;31H\u001b[38;5;252mlands. Nothing needs you right now.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[24;31H\u001b[K\n\t\u001b[38;5;243m· ⟲ 60k cached · saved $0.0020\u001b[m\u001b[26;31H  \u001b[38;5;243m· ◆ started \u001b[38;5;146;4m@bui