[259.535805, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[6;31H\u001b[38;5;252mprints\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\n\u001b[Z\u001b[38;5;102m▏\u001b[38;5;255;48;5;234m beans: 0\u001b[96X\u001b[m\u001b[9;33H\u001b[38;5;102m▏\u001b[38;5;255;48;5;234m rice: 2\u001b[97X\u001b[m\u001b[10;33H\u001b[K\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;252mexit 0. Default threshold is 3, strictly below, so \u001b[48;5;234mtea,5\u001b[49m is correctly absent. Change the\u001b[m\u001b[12;31H\u001b[38;5;252mcutoff with e.g. \u001b[48;5;234mpython3 \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1597/project/pantry.py\u0007pantry.py\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1597/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 --threshold 5\u001b[49m. Output is sorted\u001b[m\u001b[13;31H\u001b[38;5;252malphabetically by item, one \u001b[48;5;234m<item>: <quantity>\u001b[49m per qualifying line.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[14;33H\u001b[K\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;252;1mTest result:\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[17;33H\u001b[38;5;102m▏\u001b[38;5;255;48;5;234m python3 -m unittest -v \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1597/project/test_pantry.py\u0007test_pantry.py\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[67X\u001b[m\u001b[19;31H\u001b[38;5;252m→ 9 tests, all OK (strict-below boundary, ordering, default threshold, custom threshold,\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[20;31H\u001b[38;5;252mtwo malformed-row shapes, bad header, empty result, input file unchanged).\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[21;33H\u001b[33X\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;252;1mRemaining limitations\u001b[22m (review-only; no code changed):\u001b[m\u001b[55X\u001b[24;31H\u001b[38;5;102m·\u001b[38;5;252m Test-suite gaps, not bugs: the malformed tests assert exit \u001b[48;5;234m!= 0\u001b[49m rather than pinning\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[25;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  exit \u001b[48;5;234m2\u001b[49m, and there's no test for a missing file, a blank item, or a non-integer\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[26;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  \u001b[48;5;234m--threshold\u001b[49m. The reviewer exercised all of these and the code handles them correctly\u001b[m\u001b[27;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  (exit 2, stderr message, empty stdout).\u001b[m\u001b[28;31H\u001b[38;5;102m·\u001b[38;5;252m \"Alphabetical\" is case-sensitive codepoint order (\u001b[48;5;234mApple\u001b[49m before \u001b[48;5;234mapple\u001b[49m) — the one\u001b[m\u001b[29;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  genuine spec ambiguity, resolved as case-sensitive.\u001b[m\u001b[30;31H\u001b[38;5;102m·\u001b[38;5;252m Duplicate items are listed per row, not aggregated.\u001b[m\u001b[31;31H\u001b[38;5;102m·\u001b[38;5;252m Bad input (malformed row, bad header, non-integer \u001b[48;5;234m--threshold\u001b[49m, missing file) all exit\u001b[m\u001b[32;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  2 with the message on stderr and empty stdout — the report is buffered until every row\u001b[m\u001b[33;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  parses, so there is never a partial list.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[34;31H\u001b[38;5;102m·\u001b[38;5;252m Read-only holds: \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1597/project/pantry.csv\u0007pantry.csv\u001b[24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 is byte-identical (sha256 39a54ef5…) before and after a\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[35;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  run, with no write-back/apply/mutation feature anywhere — all buying and inventory\u001b[m\u001b[36;31H\u001b[38;5;252m  edits stay manual.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[39;32H\u001b[?25h"]
