iewer\u001b[m\u001b[21;31H\u001b[38;5;252mconfirmed a negative count can never surface as a \u001b[48;5;234mbuy N\u001b[49m, in either mode.\u001b[m\u001b[22;33H\u001b[65X\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;252;1mTests:\u001b[22m \u001b[48;5;234mpython3 -m unittest -v \u001b[4m\u001b]8;;file:///tmp/caf-extended-1597/project/test_pantry.py\u0007test_pantry.py\u001b[49;24m\u001b]8;;\u0007 → 16 tests, all OK (shopping amounts\u001b[m\u001b[24;31H\u001b[38;5;252mdefault and custom threshold, shopping ordering, default-unchanged, negative rejected in\u001b[m\u001b[25;31H\u001b[38;5;252mboth modes, read-only before/after, strict boundary, empty result).\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[26;33H\u001b[K\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;252;1mReviewer's only note:\u001b[22m the three generic malformed-input tests assert \u001b[48;5;234mrc != 0\u001b[49m rather than\u001b[m\u001b[28;31H\u001b[38;5;252mpinning the spec's exact \u001b[48;5;234mrc == 2\u001b[49m (the code does return 2, verified). That's a\u001b[m\u001b[29;31H\u001b[38;5;252mtest-strength gap, not a bug; the two new negative-stock tests do pin \u001b[48;5;234m== 2\u001b[49m. Minor\u001b[m\u001b[30;31H\u001b[38;5;252munrequired gaps: no test for a nonexistent file, blank item, or non-integer \u001b[48;5;234m--threshold\u001b[m\u001b[31;31H\u001b[38;5;252m— reviewer exercised all three and they behave correctly. README carries real observed\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[32;31H\u001b[38;5;252mexamples for default, \u001b[48;5;234m--shopping\u001b[49m, and \u001b[48;5;234m--threshold 1\u001b[49m.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[33;33H\u001b[K\n\b\b\u001b[38;5;252mOne interpretation I fixed on your behalf: negative stock is rejected in both modes, not\u001b[m\u001b[35;31H\u001b[38;5;252mjust under \u001b[48;5;234m--shopping\u001b[49m. Say the word if you wanted it rejected only when shopping.\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[36;33H\u001b[38;5;103mWorking\u001b[38;5;243m checking\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;66H\u001b[38;5;243m \u001b[m   \u001b[38;5;243m$0.08 · ⟲ saved $0.0303 · 86% cached   48